1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
The payment tool says ok.
Did the payment happen?

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Here, it did not:
the database holds no payment.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Same request, same reply, four possible realities.
The agent has to tell them apart.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000
An agent that trusts the reply falsely completes
on every task where the ok hides a missing payment.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:45,000
One that retries blindly pays twice
when the first payment did go through.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The trained agent pays, reads the payment back,
finds nothing, and pays again with the same key.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:15,000
When the reply was a timeout but the payment committed,
it reads back, finds it, and does not pay again.

8
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Registered P1, 450 frozen tasks, three seeds:
0.513 to 0.772 with recovery demonstrations, 0.819 with GRPO on top.

9
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Against blind retry, duplicate mutations fall from 0.191 to 0.024.
Fewer unnecessary retries is not shown, so that registered test fails.

10
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Randomised demonstrations lift renamed tools from 0.137 to 0.741,
and an unseen workflow from 0.268 to 0.842.

11
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:58,000
What did not work: when evidence cannot settle the outcome,
the agent rarely escalates (0.050).

12
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:15,000
No-std GRPO did not help. Healthcare transfer is negative.
LLM judges are not verifier-grade.

13
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Models, traces, the live demo and the code are public.
Every number has one file and one command.

14
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:45,000
ActionProof: transaction-aware recovery under ambiguous execution.
Not a new RL optimizer, and not a claim of universal safety.
